+	PyMTP is a pythonic wrapper around libmtp, making it a bit more
+	friendly to use in python
+
+	Example Usage (or see examples/):
+		>>> import pymtp
+		>>> mtp = pymtp.MTP()
+	        >>> mtp.connect()
+		PTP: Opening session
+	        >>> print mtp.get_devicename()
+	        Device name
+	        >>> mtp.disconnect()
+		PTP: Closing session
+		>>>
